# TypeScript (recap-engine)

Follow `recap-engine/biome.json`: single quotes, semicolons always, trailing commas, 2-space indent, line width 100.

## Naming

- Modules: `camelCase.ts` (`storyItems.ts`, not `story-items.ts`)
- Components / types: `PascalCase`
- Runtime enums used as discriminants: prefix `E` (`ESceneType`, `EPlayerActionType`)
- String unions without runtime values: plain `type`, not `enum`
- Generics for payload data: always `TData`, not `D` / `T`
- Enum members and wire strings: one convention per domain — do not mix `Goto`/`GoTo` or `goto`/`go_to`

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — inconsistent member + wire value across packages
enum ESceneActionType { Goto = 'goto' }
enum EPlayerActionType { GoTo = 'go_to' }

// ✅ GOOD — aligned naming
enum EPlayerActionType { GoTo = 'go_to' }
```

## Types

- Prefer `export type FooProps = { ... }` over `interface` unless declaration merging is needed
- Use `import type` for type-only imports
- Discriminated unions: switch must be exhaustive with `never` in `default`
- No identity aliases (`type Value<T> = T`) and no unused type parameters
- Named constants instead of magic numbers (`DEFAULT_MOTION_DURATION_MS = 420`)

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
default: {
  const _exhaustive: never = action;
  return _exhaustive;
}
```
